# Keep the Docker build context small. Without this file the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` sends the ENTIRE
# `target/` directory on any host with a built workspace (every dev machine, and any CI runner that caches
# target/ between runs): tens of GB, all of it irrelevant, since the builder stage runs its own
# `cargo build --release` from scratch.
target/
.git/

# Solana program build artifacts (irrelevant to this image — see the Dockerfile's own header
# comment: scoped to `-p rome-zk-sequencer`, not `programs/*`, which need `cargo build-sbf`'s own
# toolchain).
programs/*/target/

# Local-only, never meant to reach an image.
*.log
.DS_Store

# The operator's own state under deploy/rollup: payer and sequencer keys, rendered configs (database password, jwt
# secret), .env, chain.toml, the verification key and the guest ELF. The image copies none of it.
deploy/rollup/keys/
deploy/rollup/rendered/
deploy/rollup/.env
deploy/rollup/chain.toml
deploy/rollup/vkey.json
deploy/rollup/elf/
